      walkthrough = "**Level:** 100\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nThis is the starting task of the 25th Anniversary. You can obtain it from Alta the Frightened in Crescent Reach. She is on the Find tool (Ctrl-F).\n/waypoint -1165, -1474, -55\nYou say, 'Hail, Alta the Frightened'\nAlta the Frightened says, 'No, no... they feel all [wrong].'\nYou say, 'What is wrong?'\nAlta the Frightened says, 'The baby dragons. They are everywhere, but they are also... [not here]. Their nonexistent presence is an affront to our great Mother Veeshan.'\nYou say, 'What do you mean not here?'\nAlta the Frightened says, 'Exactly that! Other things about it are off as well. Colors. Voices. Things are wrong! I swear it. It wasn't just me, there was [another].'\nYou say, 'Another who saw the baby dragons?'\nAlta the Frightened says, 'He preceded the not-dragons, yet spoke endlessly of them. It is probably why he was in Crescent Reach. To [find them]...'\nYou say, ''Find them'? But there a lot of dragons here already.'\nAlta the Frightened says, 'He muttered something about the gnolls, that maybe the gnolls were shown them.' His eyes widen. 'Shown them! Shown them as I have been shown them. The gnolls may know more! It is all wrong... Will you [look for him]?'\nYou say, 'I can look for him.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Chasing What's Not Real'.\nAlta the Frightened says, 'Thank you! Thank you, thank you, thank you...'\nVisions of dragons, baby dragons, have been spotted. A fearful Drakkin has requested your assistance in unreaveling this mystery.\nAlta stated a gentleman was muttering about dragons, and that perhaps the gnolls were shown his vision.\n1. Seek a clue among the gnolls - 0/1 - ALL\nThis step was very vague and took me just blind luck clicking on objects on the ground in areas where gnolls are near where the baby dragons are at which I found in Blackburrow.\nIn Blackburrow at /waypoint +80, -193 in one of the little cubby areas on the way to Everfrost peaks there is a small hatchet on the ground. Loot it. They respawn quickly.\nThis axe was discarded quickly, and touching it pushes an echo through your mind: A swing. The axe failed to meet its target, yet there was no fault in the aim. Another swing, another failed connection. Did the blade pass through the small dragon? Beside the axe is a small twig of Luclin-daylight origin, yet not wild. Cultivated, perhaps? What an odd find.\nYour task 'Chasing What's Not Real' has been updated.\n2. Seek a clue among Luclin's daytime flora - 0/1 - ALL\nQuest Text: The axe found in Blackburrow provided the following echo:\nA swing. The axe failed to meet its target, yet there was no fault in the aim. Another swing, another failed connection. Did the blade pass through the small dragon? Besides the axe is a small twig of Luclin-daylight origin, yet not wild. Cultivated, perhaps? What an off find.\nAnother vague step. This is found in Sanctus Seru in an area where there is a walk way with some bushes and some guards in the northwest part of the zone, you'll see a baby dragon. The plant you are looking for is the smallest out of the all in the southeast corner of that area at /waypoint +441, +564, +60. The plant looks like it has blue flowers in it and almost blends into the grass.\nClick on it to receive the update.\nThis bush is out of place compared to the others, its colors counter the uniform appearance of the rest of the Sanctus Seru park. Touching the bush sends another echo, reverberating: Was he intoxicated, or was it just the visions of dragons? This bush, its colorful branches would make an absolutely glorious bouquet. Branches? In a bouquet? It shall be offered to the dragons. The bloody wine cork beneath the bush seems out of place for Sanctus Seru. Where would someone serve wine like blood?\nYour task 'Chasing What's Not Real' has been updated.\n3. Seek a clue where wine like blood may flow - 0/1 - ALL\nQuest Text: The mismatched bush in Sanctus Seru provided the following echo:\nWas he intoxicated, or was it just the visions of dragons? This bush, its colorful branches would make an absolutely glorious bouquet. Branches? In a bouquet? It shall be offered to the dragons. The bloody wine cork beneath the bush seems out of place for Sanctus Seru. Where would someone serve wine like blood?\nThis step is in Dreadspire Keep at /waypoint +3486, +4, +102 in the dining room on a big table. It's a bottle of wine.\nThe deep red color of this wine makes it difficult to determine if the wine is of the vine or of the vein. It doesn't appear to be the only one present at this dinner party, a popular vintage amongst its mixed company of living and not-so-living. Yet, it too holds an echo, far more faint than the others: Dragons? In Mayong's own Norrathian stronghold? Babies, how mad! It's time to get ready for a dinner party.\nMistmoore Hostess says, 'Oh, that's not for YOU, silly. That was saved for our friend. Our friend. Our friend. Our friend with the dragons. Why did he have dragons?' She suddenly gets very angry, eyes alight with madness. 'Dragons aren't allowed here!'\nMistmoore Hostess says, 'Dragons, dragons, dragorn, dragorn. The friend was going to pay them for something. One gold coin for... dragons? Dragons. Our friend. Into the bloooooooodfields.'\nYour task 'Chasing What's Not Real' has been updated.\n4. Seek a clue in the Bloodfields - 0/1 - The Bloodfields\nQuest Text: The blood wine in Mayong's Dreadspire Keep provided the following echo:\n'Dragons, dragons, dragorn, dragorn. The friend was going to pay them for something. One gold coin for... dragons? Dragons. Out friend. Into the blooooooodfields.'\nThis is found in the Omens of War zone, The Bloodfields. You'll see the baby dragon going back and forth. What you're looking for is a gold coin ground spawn on the top of a wall near a spire portion in the middle of the zone. Not the top bridge you port in on. Go to /waypoint +611, -150, -824 .\nThis coin isn't Kuuan in nature, but rather Norrathian. Not only that, but general issue, albeit old. Why is it discarded, and here of all places? Yet touching the coin brings forth another echo: He thought maybe, just maybe, with large enough spires, someone might be able to teleport to more dragons. Yet even some of the largest spires have driven men like Greig crazy. Perhaps the great spires of Luclin have answers.\nYour task 'Chasing What's Not Real' has been updated.\n5. Seek a clue among the great spires of Luclin - 0/1 - ALL\nQuest Text: The Norrathian gold coin in the Kuuan Bloodfields provided the following echo:\nHe thought maybe, just maybe, with large enough spires, someone might be able to teleport to more dragons. Yet even some of the largest spires have driven men like Greig crazy. Perhaps the great spires of Luclin have answers.\nThis step updates in Mons Letalis on top of the platform in the south portion. You'll see a baby dragon there. Nearby is a box you click on at /waypoint +21, +523, +204 .\nThese spires did not survive the attempts made to return to teleport prior. An echo rings through a specific fragment on the ground: Confusion. The man found nothing but confusion. If not one stone, then another. If not a confused robed man, then a confused Taelosian. Is this all a GAME to you?\nYour task 'Chasing What's Not Real' has been updated.\n6. Seek a clue with a confused Taelosian - 0/1 - ALL\nThis step updates in \"Riwwi, Coliseum of Games\", in the north part of the zone in the tunnels and in the northwest corner. There is a jail cell and a rock in it at /waypoint +757, +204, -35 . Click on it.\nIniba the Confused says, 'I am not the dragon. I am not the white robed man. Maybe the Heroes preceded the dragons? Did Veeshan seed them that way? He seeks wings of his own creation. A child's tailoring plan will send him to the sky, or crashing to the waters of the Free Port.'\nYour task 'Chasing What's Not Real' has been updated.\n7. Seek a clue where one might tailor in Freeport - 0/1 - East Freeport\nQuest Text: The Stone of Confusion within the coliseum of Riwwi on Taelosia provided the following echo:\n'I am not the dragon. I am not the white robed man. Maybe the Heroes preceded the dragons? Did Veeshan seed them that way? He seeks wings of his own creation. A child's tailoring plan will send him to the sky, or crashing to the waters of the Free Port.'\nThis step updates in East Freeport at the tailoring shop \"Leather and Hide\", owned by the Tanners, at /waypoint -340, +9, +9 . The scroll is hidden behind a box up against the wall. It's not in plain sight. Click on it.\nThe tailoring pattern for dragon-like wings looks like it could have been a valid option, but there's no leather materials on Norrath that would safely keep anyone aloft, not even a small light gnome. The pattern holds an echo of something that came before: Imbued. It should be imbued! Large dragon scales would never do, but smaller ones... The largescale dragon death in certain areas of Kunark should have something deep within ancient tunnels.\nYour task 'Chasing What's Not Real' has been updated.\n8. Seek a clue within the tunnels of Kunark - 0/1 - ALL\nQuest Text: The tailoring pattern for dragon's wings found within Eastern Freeport provided the following echo:\nImbued. It should be imbued! Large dragon scales would never do, but smaller ones... The largescale dragon death in certain areas of Kunark should have something deep within ancient tunnels.\nThis step updates in the Field of Bone. The location is on the west side of this zone, in an underground area. You'll see a bowl laying on the ground near an altar at /waypoint +430, +2951, -79 . Click on it.\nThe basket might have at one point held dragon scales, yet it has been emptied recently. Someone got to it before you could. The man in the white robe? Touching the basket relays an echo: The moon. The silvery moon. Drinal calls in the silence of a divided Shar Vahl. A letter left in haste in an empty room, never reaching its destination.\nYour task 'Chasing What's Not Real' has been updated.\n9. Seek a clue within an empty room in Shar Vahl, Divided - 0/1 - Shar Vahl, Divided\nQuest Text: The empty basket of dragon scales, found in the Field of Bone on Kunark, provided the following echo:\nThe moon. The silvery moon. Drinal calls in the silence of a divided Shar Vahl. A letter left in haste in an empty room, never reaching its destination.\nHead to \"Shar Vahl, Divided\" (ToL), to /waypoint -335, +472, -159 . You're looking for a scroll on the table that has one chair in the far southwest building in the city up on the second floor in the west room. The scroll is an actual item this time, so it will go into your inventory. Right-click it while you're in \"Shar Vahl, Divided\", it won't work it you click it in other zones.\nYou receive Leave of Absence.\nThis paper looks to be from a Drinal adherent begging for a leave of absence from their priestly duties to find the source of all dragons. The echo appears trapped within the page. Taking it to Alta might shed some answers.\nYour task 'Chasing What's Not Real' has been updated.\nYou begin casting Examine Clue.\n10. Take the latest clue to Alta - 0/1 - Crescent Reach\nQuest Text: The Leave of Absence left by Drinal adherant contains an echo, but it is trapped within its confines. Taking it to Alta might shed some answers.\nGive Alta the Frightened the Leave of Absence. She returns it to you.\nYou offered 1 Leave of Absence to Alta the Frightened.\nYou have been given: Leave of Absence\nYour task 'Chasing What's Not Real' has been updated.\nAlta the Frightened says, 'This... this pointed you back here? Here, really? Drinal is not known to have any attachment to dragons or our Mother Veeshan, so I don't understand. Take this letter to the empty meeting room off the training area. It seems to point there of all places. I'd do it, but... I have seen too much already.'\nYou complete the trade with Alta the Frightened.\n11. Examine the clue within the empty meeting room - 0/1 - Crescent Reach\nQuest Text: Take the Leave of Absence to the meeting room just off the training area within Crescent Reach. It should unlock the echo.\nThis step is still in Crescent Reach. Move to /waypoint -1417, -883, +35 , which is on the second floor in far southwest big room. Stand in the middle and right click the Leave of Absence scroll.\nA man in a white robe and a bunch of baby dragons spawns and walks away. He disappears and the step updates.\nYou begin casting Examine Clue.\nOne... two... five... So many visions of baby dragons converge upon you.\nA vision of a white robed man, wielding a scythe, walks away and his laughter won't stop. It keeps going. It keeps ringing through. Laughter, dragons, laughter, dragons, it is madness.\nMadness.\nMadness.\nMadness.\nMadness until it is gone, like a blink, and you are left with the Combine sigil of Tsaph Katta in your mind.\nYour task 'Chasing What's Not Real' has been updated.\n12. Seek out and speak with the white robed man - 0/1 - ALL\nQuest Text:\nMadness.\nMadness.\nMadness until it was gone. Visions of baby dragons and a human man in white fades only in the Combine sigil of Tsaph Katta. Find the man in the white robe.\nThis step updates in Katta Castellum at /waypoint -302, +151, +69 in the big building behind the hedges. You're looking for Ghrald McMannus, who is on the second floor of that building in one of the south rooms. He is on the find tool (Ctrl-F). Hail him.\nYou say, 'Hail, Ghrald McMannus'\nGhrald McMannus furrows his brow as he turns his attention from Gaius towards the adventurer. 'You're here about the [visions] of dragons, yes?'\nYou say, 'What are the visions?'\nGhrald McMannus says, 'My friend here, Gaius, is the originator of those insistent visions. The man has always been obsessed with dragons, but I thought it a rather healthy obsession, if there ever is one. Now... he is summoning them into being, and by seeing them before him, he's feeding his visions further. Gaius [doesn't know] he's doing it.'\nYou say, 'He doesn't know? What's going on?'\nGhrald McMannus says, 'I fear it's brought on by [the gods] themselves.'\nYou say, 'The gods? Really?'\nYour task 'Chasing What's Not Real' has been updated.\nGhrald McMannus, friend of Gaius Lucianus who is facing and distributing these visions of dragons through his obsession, appreciates you finding them and has requested your help. Perhaps you both can get to the bottom of what is going on with Gaius.\nYou receive 5 silver .\nYou receive 2 gold .\nYou receive 2 platinum .\nYou received 10 Commemorative Coins.\nGhrald McMannus says, 'It has all the markings of interference by the gods: the sudden onset of symptoms, the potency of the visions, and the fact they are sticking around when my friend is no illusionist. However, the deity source is unknown. Let me think for a moment; I might have some ideas and need some help from you.'\nThis leads to the next task, Chasing Madness [quest=12897], obtained by hailing Ghrald McMannus again.\n- 2 platinum, 2 gold, 5 silver\n- 10 Commemorative Coins [item=116720]\nSubmitted by: Gidono ; Revamped by iventheassassinRewards:\n- Commemorative Coin [item=116720]\n[",
