        { name = "Deklean Korgad", change = 1 },
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n\nApparently Deklean wants proof that you can handle the terrors and also wants some liquid courage to take you to the bridge.\nGive Deklean Korgad the Fungus-covered hunk of rock, 2 Thought Horror Tentacles and a Deep Cavern Bourbon which can be purchased in Shadowhaven, Echo Caverns and the Bazaar and a few other places.\nDeklean Korgad says 'Well I'm impressed Jibbre, you actually went up against some terrors and won. I'll keep my part of the bargain and show you across the chasm. I'm warning you though, this side of the cave is a candy shop compared to the far side.Anyhow, follow me and we'll make our way there.I'm sure you'll be able to dispatch anything we run into on the way, seeing as how you're an accomplished horror slayer!'\nYour faction standing with Deklean Korgad has been adjusted by 1.\nHe then takes the most direct route to the chasm. Left alone he'll die fighting stuff. I also believe he may be susceptible to friendly fire so be careful. Not sure though.\nWhen you get to the chasm and see the fake bridge.\nDeklean Korgad says \"Well here's the chasm I told you about. Seeing as how you're not very quick, I'd expect you to go barreling across that bridge over there at full speed! That'd get you killed in a hurry. I'm sure the mushrooms would enjoy feeding off of your remains though. Hurry up there now! We haven't got all day!'\nWhen you get to the invisible bridge.\nDeklean Korgad says 'Here's where you'll have to trust me friend. Just stay close to me and you'll be fine. And be QUIET! The beasties on the other side aren't nearly as pleasant as the ones over here.'\nHe leads the way across the bridge walking. Every ten feet or so a beacon appears and lands on the bridge. They look the same as traps. I didn't try to disarm them or remove them. He leads you all the way to the other side.\nDeklean Korgad says 'Well here you are, the other side of the chasm. This is where I leave you, I need to take care of some things over here. I'm sure you'll be just fine as long as you stay quiet. Good luck to you friend.'\nHail him again to show him how quiet you are.\nYou say, 'Hail, Deklean Korgad'\nDeklean Korgad puts his hand over your mouth. 'Shuuuush! You may not be afraid of any of these beasties, but there's no reason to make all this noise and make them come running! (Diacritical mark missing here in text after the exclamation mark)\nHe remains up for a few minutes and the beacons disappear a few minutes after he vanishes.\nNothing fancy. No new toys. Not sure if there is a way to trigger the beacons. Submitted by: SeverrianRewards:\n[",
